What is the output of the following code snippet?

x = 8
if x > 5:
    if x < 10:
        print("x is a single-digit number greater than 5")
else:
    print("x is 5 or less")

What is the final output of the following code?

x = 4
if x < 5:
    x += 10
if x > 10:
    x -= 3
if x == 11:
    x *= 2
else:
    x /= 2
print(x)
